meta {
  name: Transfer - Assign Center
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/accession/transfers/{{transferId}}/assign-center
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "destinationBranchId": "{{destinationBranchId}}"
  }
}

tests {
  test("201 Created", function () { expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(201); });
}

docs {
  Set or change the destination of a transfer created without one.

  For an INTERNAL transfer this is allowed only while it is IN_TRANSIT or PICKED_UP;
  from RECEIVED onward (or once closed) it is refused with 422 TRANSFER_NOT_EDITABLE.
  Who may act (INTERNAL transfer): only the SENDING branch. The caller's active branch
  (the profile they switched to) must be the branch that sent the sample, otherwise
  403 TRANSFER_WRONG_BRANCH and nothing changes. A caller with no active branch
  (business admin) is refused too. A group Retrieve is refused as a whole, never
  skipped, when any sent sample belongs to another branch.
  Internal branch transfer rules (manager flow 2026-09-29):
  - Once a sample is SENT_INTERNAL to another branch, the SENDER's Technician
    worklist hides its report (list, counts, detail, history, every write, the five
    secondary worklists, attachments, inventory usage, analyser results). It behaves
    as "Lab report not found" (404 LAB_REPORT_NOT_FOUND) for the sender.
  - A sent sample accepts ONLY Retrieve from the sender, and only until the
    receiving branch has received it (transfer IN_TRANSIT / PICKED_UP).
  - The receiving branch's Reject / Repeat returns the test to the sender: the
    sender's original sample goes SENT_INTERNAL -> REPEAT automatically.

  **Assign Center vs Edit Center.** The same endpoint serves both: with no destination
  yet it is "Assign Center" (permission group ASSIGN_CENTER); with a destination already
  set it is "Edit Center" (UPDATE_CENTER). Allowed while the transfer is IN_TRANSIT or
  PICKED_UP, refused once the receiving branch has received it. Editing the destination
  changes the SAME transfer (nothing is deleted): it drops out of the old branch's
  Internal Transfer list and appears in the new branch's.
  `logisticsType` is optional here, but while the transfer is In-Transit with no logistics
  type the receiving branch does not see it and cannot pick it up; setting it (now or
  through a later Edit Center) makes it appear. `sendDate` / `sendTime` are written only
  when sent (the screen pre-fills the current date and time).

  **Dialog (INTERNAL).** The screen now opens a per-tube dialog: each tube has its own center,
  un-ticking a tube retrieves it, and Confirm sends one all-or-nothing request to
  `POST transfers/apply-center-changes` (see `50 Accession/45`). This single-transfer endpoint stays
  for other callers and for External / Outsource transfers.

  **Re-addressing a transfer the first branch already Picked Up.** Changing the destination of
  an INTERNAL transfer to a DIFFERENT branch while it is Picked Up starts it over: it goes back
  to IN_TRANSIT and the old pick-up (`pickedUpBy` / `pickedUpAt`) is cleared, because the new
  branch has not picked it up (it must Pick Up before it can Receive; the old branch can do
  nothing with it). Every change of destination (also a first assignment) is recorded in the same
  transaction: a row on the sender sample's history (action `assign-center`, "Center changed from
  X to Y while <stage>", plus "it had been picked up, so it starts over at In-Transit" when reset)
  and Audit-log entries (module ACCESSION, `metadata.side`): `sender` under the sending branch
  always; `old-receiver` under the old destination when it had been able to see the transfer (it
  now loses it); `new-receiver` under the new destination once it can see it (an In-Transit
  transfer needs a logistics type first). Saving the same destination again (a logistics-only
  edit) is not a re-address and writes none of this.

  **The destination must OFFER every test on the tube (Phase 1).** A tube can only go to a branch that has an
  ACTIVE Lab Test List entry for each of its tests. The match goes through the tenant test both branches copied
  (the sender's Branch Master Data test -> `sourceMasterLabTestId` -> the destination's Branch Master Data test
  with the same tenant test -> an active, not deleted list entry); any of the destination's lists counts. A test
  with no tenant link (hand-created at the branch) cannot be matched and counts as NOT offered. A free-text tube
  test (no catalogue test) is skipped. Otherwise: 422 `DESTINATION_LACKS_TEST`, "<Branch> does not offer: <tests>.
  Choose another branch." (at most five test names, then "and N more"); nothing is changed.
  Checked when the destination CHANGES (first centre or Edit Center), not on a logistics-only save that keeps the
  destination it already had. `apply-center-changes` refuses the whole batch naming the tube
  (`CENTER_CHANGES_REFUSED`, "Nothing was changed. Tube ACC-...: <Branch> does not offer: ...").

  **Outsource transfers:** the center and the logistics type set here are what unlock Pick Up (center + logistics type)
  and Receive / Accept (center) - see `TRANSFER_OUTSOURCE_NOT_ASSIGNED` on those steps. Send `logisticsType` together
  with `outsourceCenterId` (a logistics-only change needs the center again, as for the other kinds).
}
